  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "A point is chosen uniformly from a circle of radius 1. Find the probability that it is closer to the circumference than to the centre.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
      "worked": "Let $r$ be the distance of the chosen point from the centre. Its distance from the circumference is $1-r$, so it is closer to the circumference when $r>\\frac12$. The favourable region is the outer annulus.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(E)&=\\frac{\\pi(1)^2-\\pi\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2}{\\pi(1)^2}\\\\\\Pr(E)&=1-\\frac14\\\\\\Pr(E)&=\\frac34.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
  },
